1.2.5. Sum of Digits of a Five Digit Number
02:27
Write a C program that reads a five-digit integer from the user and prints the sum of its digits.



Input Format:

Input contains a single five-digit number 
.


Output Format:

Print the sum of individual digits if the input is valid (i.e., 
 has exactly 5 digits).
Print "Invalid input i"f the input is invalid (i.e., 
 does not have exactly 5 digits).


Constraints:


//write your code here..
#include <stdio.h>

void main() {
    int num, temp, sum = 0, count = 0;

    scanf("%d", &num);

    // Copy original number to temp
    temp = num;

    // Count digits
    while (temp > 0) {
        temp /= 10;
        count++;
    }

    // Check if number has exactly 5 digits
    if (count == 5) {
        temp = num;
        while (temp > 0) {
            sum += temp % 10;  // Add last digit
            temp /= 10;        // Remove last digit
        }
        printf("%d\n", sum);
    } else {
        printf("Invalid input\n");
    }


}
